      "individual_reservations": {
        "contact_volume_requirement": "The entire wetted PCB support stays inside its unchanged 4 x 4 mm land. The proposed finite fan, tip and endpoint adapter stay inside the land projection; the later insulated wire has its existing separate 3D loom envelope. Qualification must verify actual tails, solder, insulation, tool and restraint envelopes. No minimum contact conductivity or resistance acceptance follows from this geometry.",
        "factory_tool_requirement": "Factory tool, bare fan, solder and wire attachment operations remain within the individual 6 x 6 mm B-side column near the land. P must be accessible before K and its loom are installed. This is a process requirement for #65, not a claim that the installed assembly provides a tool corridor. Other boards and loose wires must be absent from the tool approach during that operation.",
        "front_face_scope": "Terminals, solder and stripped-wire fans are on B.Cu. The solid PCB separates them from F-side surface parts. Every through-hole pad/drill remains in the B-side collision authority; no through-hole or foreign via is exempted. F-side removal is not permission for a foreign conductor to enter a B-side terminal volume.",
        "rationale": "The original load-power strip was a PROPOSAL reservation for load terminals, not a retained solid part or transverse bus. All six independent wires keep their fixed endpoints and separate finite fans. Replace only the broad F/B strip with four B-side reservations matching the two existing AGND reservations. Preserve every unrelated reservation and all foreign-object prohibitions.",
        "references": [
          "TP990025",
